    "sbar": {
      "situation": "The bank system has recovered, confirmed by two clean recovery checks in a row, the last at 46 s. Screening is running on its standby, and payments errors are at 0.",
      "background": "The pipeline raised the gateway setting balance_cache_ttl_s from 0.5 to 600 s just before the alert, which would serve stale balances. Separately, the primary screening link slowed to about 1815 ms p95 against a 14 ms baseline, and the clearing worker went down with exit code 15 and 19 items queued.",
      "assessment": "Payments calls to the slow primary screening timed out (error rate 0.49 rising to 1.0), so the incident commander failed screening over to the standby, which now answers in 15 ms with payments errors at 0. The incident commander reverted gateway balance_cache_ttl_s to 0.5, and the probe shows app balances match the ledger. It also restarted the clearing worker, which had no poison message, and the worker drained its queue to 0 with network calls succeeding.",
      "recommendation": "Investigate why the primary screening link is slow before failing back to it. Find out why the pipeline changed balance_cache_ttl_s and why the clearing worker exited with code 15. Operations should review balances shown or acted on while the 600 s cache was live, and the payments that timed out during the screening slowdown."
    },
